chool Board Member Gibbon District (ISD #2365)","seats":1,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5010,"candidates":[{"name":"Kenneth Briese","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Casey Prochniak","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Gibbon-Fairfax-Winthrop","schoolNum":"2365","maybe":true},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd2365-school-board-member-fairfax-district-isd-2365","office":"School Board Member Fairfax District (ISD #2365)","category":"School Board Member Fairfax District (ISD #2365)","seats":1,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"Unopposed.","ballotOrder":5012,"candidates":[{"name":"George Grosam","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Gibbon-Fairfax-Winthrop","schoolNum":"2365","maybe":true},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd2365-school-board-member-winthrop-district-isd-2365","office":"School Board Member Winthrop District (ISD #2365)","category":"School Board Member Winthrop District (ISD #2365)","seats":1,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"Unopposed.","ballotOrder":5014,"candidates":[{"name":"Emilee Stehr","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Gibbon-Fairfax-Winthrop","schoolNum":"2365","maybe":true},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd2687-school-board-member-isd-2687-elect-3","office":"School Board Member (ISD #2687) (Elect 3)","category":"School Board Member (ISD #2687) (Elect 3)","seats":3,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5000,"candidates":[{"name":"Shannah Mulvihill","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Katie Anne Koch","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Tristin Michael Fliehe","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Howard Lake-Waverly-Winsted","schoolNum":"2687"},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd2859-school-board-member-isd-2859-elect-3","office":"School Board Member (ISD #2859) (Elect 3)","category":"School Board Member (ISD #2859) (Elect 3)","seats":3,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","ballotOrder":5000,"candidates":[{"name":"Elizabeth Griebel","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Anthony Paggen","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Chad Moser","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Sarah Hueser","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Joyce Peterson","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Donna VonBerge","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Kevin Kuester","party":null,"status":"candidate"},{"name":"Timothy Dilworth","party":null,"status":"candidate"}],"scope":"school","level":"School","area":"Glencoe-Silver Lake","schoolNum":"2859"}],"referendums":[{"id":"mn-amendment-1","name":"CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT 1: Increasing funding to school districts","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the Minnesota Constitution be amended to increase the funding going to all school districts from the permanent school fund, which is a fund that supports school districts without raising individual income or property taxes, effective July 1, 2027?"},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd0423-school-district-question-1-isd-423","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #423): Approval of School District  Referendum Revenue Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 423 (Hutchinson Public Schools) has proposed to increase its general education revenue by $412 per pupil. The proposed referendum revenue authorization would be applicable for ten years beginning with taxes payable in 2027 unless otherwise revoked or reduced as provided by law.\n\nShall the increase in the revenue proposed by the school board of Independent School District No. 423 be approved?","schoolNum":"0423","area":"Hutchinson"},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd0465-school-district-question-1-isd-465","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #465): Approval of School District Referendum Revenue Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 465 (Litchfield Public Schools) has proposed to increase its general education revenue by $415 per pupil.  The proposed referendum revenue authorization would be applicable for ten years beginning with taxes payable in 2027, and increase each year by the rate of inflation beginning with taxes payable in 2028, unless otherwise revoked or reduced as provided by law.\n\nShall the increase in the revenue proposed by the school board of Independent School District No. 465 be approved?\n\nBY VOTING \"YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING FOR A PROPERTY TAX INCREASE.","schoolNum":"0465","area":"Litchfield"},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd0465-school-district-question-2-isd-465","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 2 (ISD #465): Approval of School District Bond Issue","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the school board of Independent School District No. 465 (Litchfield Public Schools) also be authorized to issue its general obligation school building bonds in an amount not to exceed $15,400,000 to provide funds for the acquisition and betterment of school sites and facilities, including the construction of improvements, renovations and upgrades to the Wagner Education Building, including the construction of a secure entrance, parking lot expansion, boiler replacement, the acquisition and installation of a new fire suppression system, and updates to rest rooms^ renovations and updates to the High School/Middle School site and facility, including the remodeling of locker rooms and the construction of ADA accessibility renovations to special education spaces^ the construction of mechanical, HVAC and lighting updates to school sites and facilities^ and the construction of repairs to the grandstand to the football stadium?\n\nBY VOTING \"YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING FOR A PROPERTY TAX INCREASE.","schoolNum":"0465","area":"Litchfield"},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd2365-school-district-question-1-isd-2365","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #2365): Approval of Capital Project Levy Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 2365 (Gibbon-Fairfax-Winthrop) has proposed a capital project levy authorization in the amount of 1.53% times the net tax capacity of the School District. The proposed capital project levy authorization will raise approximately $400,000 for taxes payable in 2027, the first year it is to be levied, and would be authorized for ten (10) years. The estimated total cost of the projects to be funded over that time period is approximately $4,000,000. The additional revenue from the proposed authorization will be used to provide funds for the acquisition and maintenance of software, technology, and technology systems, and to pay the costs of technology-related personnel and training^ the purchase and replacement of school buses and school-related transportation vehicles^ and the acquisition of curriculum, textbooks, and materials. The projects to be funded have received a positive Review and Comment from the Commissioner of Education.\n\nShall the capital project levy proposed by the school board of lndependent School District No. 2365 be approved?\n\nBY VOTING \"YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING FOR A PROPERTY TAX INCREASE.","schoolNum":"2365","area":"Gibbon-Fairfax-Winthrop"},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd2365-school-district-question-2-isd-2365","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 2 (ISD #2365): Approval of School District Bond Issue","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"If School District Question 1 is approved, shall the school board of Independent School District No. 2365 (Gibbon-Fairfax-Winthrop) also be authorized to issue its general obligation school building bonds in an amount not to exceed $3,200,000 to provide funds for the acquisition and betterment of school sites and facilities, including the demolition of decommissioned school buildings?\n\nBY VOTING \"YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING FOR A PROPERTY TAX INCREASE.","schoolNum":"2365","area":"Gibbon-Fairfax-Winthrop"},{"id":"mn-mcleod-sd2859-school-district-question-1-isd-2859","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #2859): Revoking Existing Referendum Revenue Authorization^  Approving New Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 2859 (Glencoe-Silver Lake Public Schools) has proposed to revoke the school districts existing referendum revenue authorization of $601.98 per pupil and to replace that authorization with a new authorization of $1,445 per pupil. The proposed referendum revenue authorization would be applicable for ten years commencing with taxes payable in 2027, and increase each year by the rate of inflation beginning with taxes payable in 2028, unless otherwise revoked or reduced as provided by law.\n\nShall the school districts existing referendum revenue authorization be revoked, and the increase in the revenue proposed by the school board of Independent School District No. 2859 be approved?","schoolNum":"2859","area":"Glencoe-Silver Lake"}]}